  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: Acute dizziness with spinning sensation (vertigo), unsteadiness on standing/walking, and ear buzzing (tinnitus). Symptoms started about 2 hours ago and have been continuous; previously had a similar, shorter episode about a month ago.\n- Symptoms details: Room feels like it is moving; nausea present; no fever; no ear pain or discharge; hearing described as intact; no limb weakness; no reported headaches. Prior episode lasted ~5–10 minutes in the past.\n- Onset/duration: Sudden onset during breakfast; current vertigo is ongoing for ~2 hours.\n- Aggravating/relieving factors: Spinning worse with movement/ambulation; no explicit triggers beyond position, no relief reported.\n- Past medical history: Premature ovarian failure; on hormone replacement therapy (HRT).\n- Medications/allergies: HRT; no listed drug allergies.\n- Family/social history: Not described.\n- Vitals/exam findings: Not provided in transcript; clinician planned to check blood pressure and perform a bedside exam and ear inspection.\n- Labs/imaging: None mentioned.\n- Initial working diagnosis mentioned by physician: labyrinthitis (infectious/inflammatory inner-ear process) with plan for symptomatic treatment and formal ear examination.",
